# Water wheel of the old Kornmuehle in Brunnwinkl (house 1): an overshot
# wheel, wood o/O/l (lit top left), 16 buckets and 8 spokes around an iron hub
# (i/m/d + w glint), turning clockwise half a bucket (11.25 deg) per frame, so the 4-frame loop
# turns 45 deg and rim, buckets and spokes all loop seamlessly. An open wooden
# trough (t water surface with an s glint over the o rim, O/l side; no k over
# the water) on a post brings the mill race in from the right;
# its water t/T (s glints) pours onto the wheel with w drops. k outline (front
# layer). Generated by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grids
# below are the source.
sprite = muehlrad
size   = 48x48
origin = 24,48
anim   = turn frames=4 ticks=12 loop
